  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 74,
  "title": "Psalms 74",
  "display_title": "Psalms 74",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 74,
  "sortOrder": 19074,
  "verseCount": 23,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "O God, why hast thou cast us off for ever? why doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Remember thy congregation, which thou hast purchased of old; the rod of thine inheritance, which thou hast redeemed; this mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual desolations; even all that the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Thine enemies roar in the midst of thy congregations; they set up their ensigns for signs.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "A man was famous according as he had lifted up axes upon the thick trees.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "But now they break down the carved work thereof at once with axes and hammers.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "They have cast fire into thy sanctuary, they have defiled by casting down the dwelling place of thy name to the ground.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They said in their hearts, Let us destroy them together: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "We see not our signs: there is no more any prophet: neither is there among us any that knoweth how long.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "O God, how long shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even thy right hand? pluck it out of thy bosom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For God is my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou brakest the heads of the dragons in the waters.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces, and gavest him to be meat to the people inhabiting the wilderness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Thou didst cleave the fountain and the flood: thou driedst up mighty rivers.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Remember this, that the enemy hath reproached, O LORD, and that the foolish people have blasphemed thy name.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "O deliver not the soul of thy turtledove unto the multitude of the wicked: forget not the congregation of thy poor for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Have respect unto the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of cruelty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Arise, O God, plead thine own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee daily.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:74:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Forget not the voice of thine enemies: the tumult of those that rise up against thee increaseth continually.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 74:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:74:23"
      }
    }
  ],
